stremio (4.4.181-orp4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add the pinned libmpv gpu-next render-API backend on top of the RK3588 mpv fork.
  * Make Stremio request gpu-next while retaining direct V4L2-request hardware decode.
  * Keep Main10/NV15 frames in DRM PRIME instead of using the failed copy-back path.
  * Target green/corrupt 4K HEVC Main10 Dolby Vision rendering seen on RK3588.

 -- stremio-Opi5-Armbian maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:30:00 +0100

stremio (4.4.181-orp3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Prefer v4l2request-copy for Stremio's embedded libmpv renderer.
  * Keep RK3588 VPU decoding while avoiding direct packed NV15 DRM-PRIME import.
  * Retain direct v4l2request and normal safe hardware methods as fallbacks.
  * Target green/corrupt rendering observed during 4K runtime validation.

 -- stremio-Opi5-Armbian maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0100

stremio (4.4.181-orp2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Bundle a private pinned FFmpeg/libmpv stack under /opt/stremio/rk3588.
  * Enable the RK3588 V4L2-request hardware-decoding userspace path.
  * Keep private multimedia libraries isolated from system package libraries.
  * Validate private libmpv/libavcodec linkage in native ARM64 CI.

 -- stremio-Opi5-Armbian maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:30:00 +0100

stremio (4.4.181-orp1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build the official Stremio 4.4.181 shell natively for Ubuntu 26.04 ARM64.
  * Use Ubuntu's system libmpv and generated shared-library dependencies.
  * Remove the obsolete explicit librubberband2 package dependency.

 -- stremio-Opi5-Armbian maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0100
